From 329a740e979b505bfb1f6a9509113edceb004026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:30:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TFEL: device code support of finite strain tools, rotations
 and slip systems

- fixed size arrays (`GenericFixedSizeArray`) use the implicit copy and move
  operations, so that tensors are trivially copyable;
- `TrivialGenTypeBase`, a tagged union of trivially copyable types with the
  interface of `GenTypeBase`, without `std::variant` (not supported in
  device code by nvc++), used by `FiniteStrainBehaviourTangentOperator`;
- finite strain tools usable in device code: tangent operator conversions,
  `LogarithmicStrainHandler` (header only), tiny matrix solvers and
  inversion without exceptions in device code, derivatives of isotropic
  functions, stensor products, `st2tost2::fromRotationMatrix`;
- `change_basis` for `tvector<N>` and `tmatrix<N, N>`, consistent with the
  rotation of symmetric tensors;
- `tfel::utilities::getConstantObject`: objects built at compile time
  usable in host and device code (`__device__ constexpr` variables with
  CUDA and HIP, copies with nvc++ -stdpar=gpu);
- `MetallicCFCSlidingSystems` built at compile time and
  `MetallicCFCGenericSlidingSystemsInteractionMatrix` computed at each call
  (the matrix was previously cached at the first call);
- attribute lists placed before `TFEL_HOST_DEVICE` (clang CUDA rejects
  `__host__ __device__ [[nodiscard]]`);
- unit tests: `TrivialGenTypeBaseTest`, `ChangeBasisTest`.
